  {:repo "orgs/cloud-itonami/data-center-ops"
   :label "data-center-ops actor gate and the payload it must not drop"
   :cmd ["nbb" "test/data_center_ops/murakumo_test.cljs"]
   :green-marker "0 failures, 0 errors"
   ;; murakumo.cljc is the only executable code in that repo and it is a gate:
   ;; it turns a request into :mst/put-record effects and nothing downstream
   ;; re-derives them. Until 2026-08-30 it had no tests at all, and writing them
   ;; found two silent losses -- `records` given as a vector fell through to {}
   ;; while the plan stayed :ready, and the caller's record was merged over the
   ;; actor's own fields, so it could name a different actorDid or claim a
   ;; different $type than the collection it was filed under.
   ;;
   ;; Runs on nbb, no JVM: the source is .cljc with zero reader conditionals,
   ;; so one runtime executes all of it and there is no second branch here that
   ;; could rot unseen.
   ;;
   ;; All twelve below were applied one at a time at pin e269e978 on 2026-08-30,
   ;; each anchor unique in the file, each reddening the tests named and **no
   ;; others** (the replay compared the full set of red test names against
   ;; :must-fail, not just its presence), with the unmutated tree green before
   ;; the battery and after it.
   ;;
   ;; `refusal-reason-renamed` is here for the rule that a negative test must
   ;; refuse for the reason it names: it leaves the throw in place and only
   ;; changes the keyword, so a test that merely observed "something was thrown"
   ;; would survive it. It does not.
   :mutations
   [{:id :dco/gate-stops-checking
     :why "the gate stops asking -- the shape a check takes when somebody neuters the filter. Nothing may be emitted before every constitutional gate attests; this is the invariant the whole actor pattern rests on"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "(remove #(boolean (gate-value attestations %)))"
     :replace "(remove (constantly true))"
     :must-fail ["no-attestations-blocks-and-emits-nothing"
                 "absent-attestations-block-rather-than-default-open"
                 "partial-attestation-blocks-and-names-only-the-missing-gates"
                 "explicit-false-is-not-an-attestation"
                 "no-cell-can-be-planned-without-attestations"
                 "gates-are-checked-before-the-payload"]}

    {:id :dco/presence-read-as-attestation
     :why "read the gate as present rather than as attesting -- a plausible refactor that makes a gate answered `false` count as attested, and drops the string-keyed spelling callers use"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "(remove #(boolean (gate-value attestations %)))"
     :replace "(remove #(contains? attestations %))"
     :must-fail ["explicit-false-is-not-an-attestation"
                 "attestations-are-read-from-every-shape-the-callers-use"]}

    {:id :dco/sequential-records-dropped
     :why "restores the original silent loss: `records` written as a vector falls through to {} while the plan stays :ready, so the host is handed a well-formed instruction to write a record with no payload in it and reports success"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "(sequential? records) (vec records)"
     :replace "(sequential? records) {}"
     :must-fail ["payload-survives-every-accepted-records-shape"]}

    {:id :dco/unusable-shape-guard-disabled
     :why "disables the refusal so an unusable shape is dropped again instead of raised. Dropping and refusing look identical downstream -- both produce a successful put-record -- which is why the drop went unnoticed for as long as it did"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "(some? records)       (throw (ex-info"
     :replace "(some? nil)           (throw (ex-info"
     :must-fail ["unusable-records-shape-is-refused-not-silently-dropped"]}

    {:id :dco/refusal-reason-renamed
     :why "leaves the throw and renames only the reason. A test that asserted merely that something was thrown would survive this; pinning the literal is what makes the assertion about this refusal rather than about any failure"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find ":reason :records/unusable-shape"
     :replace ":reason :records/bad"
     :must-fail ["unusable-records-shape-is-refused-not-silently-dropped"]}

    {:id :dco/provenance-forgeable-again
     :why "restores the original merge order, in which the caller's record overrode the actor's own fields. A record could then name a different actorDid, or claim a $type other than the collection it is filed under -- which is what an ATProto consumer dispatches on -- and the store has no way to detect it afterwards"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "(merge defaults\n                            (assert-provenance! asserted supplied)\n                            asserted)"
     :replace "(merge defaults\n                            asserted\n                            supplied)"
     :must-fail ["caller-cannot-forge-actor-provenance"]}

    {:id :dco/refusal-does-not-name-the-field
     :why "the refusal stops saying which field was forged. An operator reading only the message cannot tell whether the actorDid or the scaffold flag was the one that moved"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find ":field k"
     :replace ":field :some-field"
     :must-fail ["caller-cannot-forge-actor-provenance"]}

    {:id :dco/actor-did-drifts-from-manifest
     :why "the DID the records are signed with drifts from the one actor-manifest.jsonld advertises. Both files already disagree with .well-known/did.json, so this pair is the one that still holds and the only guard against it widening"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "\"did:web:data-center-ops.etzhayyim.com\")"
     :replace "\"did:web:data-center-ops.example.com\")"
     :must-fail ["actor-did-agrees-with-the-published-manifest"]}

    {:id :dco/record-type-stops-matching-collection
     :why "$type stops naming the collection the record is written into. Both values are plausible strings and the effect still looks well-formed, so nothing but this assertion distinguishes them"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find ":$type coll\n                       :actorDid actor-did"
     :replace ":$type (:legacy-cell spec)\n                       :actorDid actor-did"
     :must-fail ["record-type-matches-the-collection-it-is-written-into"]}

    {:id :dco/empty-record-key-allowed
     :why "an empty record key reaches the store. An empty rkey addresses the collection itself rather than a record in it, and the fallback exists precisely to keep that from happening"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "(if (str/blank? clean) \"unknown\" clean)"
     :replace "clean"
     :must-fail ["an-empty-record-key-becomes-unknown-rather-than-empty"]}

    {:id :dco/cells-share-one-collection
     :why "every cell writes into one shared collection, so the 25 cells overwrite each other's records. The effects still look correct one at a time -- only comparing them reveals it"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "(str \"com.etzhayyim.data-center-ops.\" name))"
     :replace "(str \"com.etzhayyim.data-center-ops.cell\"))"
     :must-fail ["each-cell-writes-its-own-collection"]}

    {:id :dco/a-cell-quietly-exempted-from-a-gate
     :why "one cell is given a shorter gate list than the rest. It still blocks with no attestations, so the gate tests stay green; only the declaration check sees that :incident now requires less of itself than its 24 siblings do"
     :file "src/data_center_ops/murakumo.cljc"
     :find ":incident {:legacy-cell \"com-etzhayyim-apps-dataCenterOps-incident\"\n     :phase :event\n     :murakumo-node \"reuben\"\n     :collections [(collection \"incident\")]\n     :required-gates common-gates"
     :replace ":incident {:legacy-cell \"com-etzhayyim-apps-dataCenterOps-incident\"\n     :phase :event\n     :murakumo-node \"reuben\"\n     :collections [(collection \"incident\")]\n     :required-gates (rest common-gates)"
     :must-fail ["every-cell-declares-the-common-gates-and-one-collection"]}]}

  {:repo "orgs/cloud-itonami/app-public-domain-colorization"
   :label "lg-pd-color — portability, the error envelope, and the BPMN rights gate"
   ;; This port declared `bb` as the only way to run its tests, in a `bb.edn`
   ;; naming the pre-rename `com-junkawasaki/langgraph-clj`. `bb` is the script
   ;; host ADR-2607173000 retired, so the only runtime that had ever executed
   ;; these `.cljc` namespaces was the JVM one -- and they were not portable at
   ;; all: `graphs/task.cljc` caught `Exception` and called `.getMessage`, so
   ;; under nbb the namespace could not be READ. Nothing reported it, because
   ;; nothing ran it. `run_tests.cljs` now runs both runtimes and prints the
   ;; marker only when both are green, which is what the first mutation exists
   ;; to keep true.
   ;;
   ;; Three kinds of thing are shot at here, because this suite guards three:
   ;;   1. the code            (lg-clj/src/lg_pd_color/**)
   ;;   2. the process data    (bpmn/colorize-public-domain-work.bpmn)
   ;;   3. the two runtime configs (lg-clj/nbb.edn vs lg-clj/deps.edn)
   ;; A suite that only reddens on (1) is a test of itself, not of the pipeline
   ;; -- the rights gate lives entirely in (2), in one XML attribute per gate.
   ;;
   ;; All eleven were applied one at a time at pin 25cd2fce on 2026-08-30, with
   ;; the tree restored between runs; each reddened the tests naming it, and the
   ;; unmutated control was green before the battery and after it.
   :cmd ["nbb" "run_tests.cljs"]
   :green-marker "lg-pd-color: both runtimes green (nbb + JVM)"
   :mutations
   [{:id :pdcolor/portable-not-jvm-only
     :why "the `.cljc` really runs on both runtimes. Reverting to JVM interop does not fail a test -- it stops nbb from READING the namespace, which is why the defect survived from the extraction until 2026-08-30. The marker names a diagnostic string rather than a test name for exactly that reason: there is no test result to name when the load itself dies"
     :file "lg-clj/src/lg_pd_color/graphs/task.cljc"
     :find "(catch #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n          {:error (clip (error-message e) 300)})"
     :replace "(catch Exception e\n          {:error (clip (.getMessage e) 300)})"
     :must-fail ["Unable to resolve symbol: Exception"]}

    {:id :pdcolor/error-message-unclipped
     :why "the 300-char clip the node docstring claims. An unbounded handler message otherwise lands verbatim in an HTTP body -- ffmpeg stderr is not small"
     :file "lg-clj/src/lg_pd_color/graphs/task.cljc"
     :find "(clip (error-message e) 300)"
     :replace "(error-message e)"
     :must-fail ["error-message-is-clipped-to-300-chars"]}

    {:id :pdcolor/boundary-handler-goes-quiet
     :why "an unbound native handler fails loud. Returning {} instead makes a deploy that forgot to inject a handler report 200 with an empty output -- a restoration step that did nothing, recorded as done"
     :file "lg-clj/src/lg_pd_color/graphs/task.cljc"
     :find "  (fn [_kwargs]\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"native worker handler not configured: \" name\n                         \" (inject via lg-pd-color.graphs.task/*handlers*)\")\n                    {:handler name}))))"
     :replace "  (fn [_kwargs] {}))"
     :must-fail ["every-task-graph-fails-loud-when-its-handler-is-unbound"]}

    {:id :pdcolor/unmapped-nsid-echoed-whole
     :why "the caller-supplied NSID is clipped before it goes into an error body. The clip is the only bound on what an unmapped caller can push back through this surface"
     :file "lg-clj/src/lg_pd_color/server.cljc"
     :find "(str \"NSID not mapped: \" (clip nsid 120))"
     :replace "(str \"NSID not mapped: \" nsid)"
     :must-fail ["an-unmapped-nsid-is-not-echoed-back-unbounded"]}

    {:id :pdcolor/assistant-id-default-dropped
     :why "server.py's documented default. A client that omits assistant_id must get liveness, not a 404 -- the 404 reads as `this deployment is broken`"
     :file "lg-clj/src/lg_pd_color/server.cljc"
     :find "(or (:assistant_id body) \"health\")"
     :replace "(:assistant_id body)"
     :must-fail ["runs-without-an-assistant-id-is-health"]}

    {:id :pdcolor/graph-renamed-without-the-bpmn
     :why "a graph renamed here without the BPMN following. The dispatch surface stays perfectly consistent with itself; the process keeps dispatching a Zeebe task type nobody serves, and the run does not fail -- it stalls in the broker"
     :file "lg-clj/src/lg_pd_color/graphs/task.cljc"
     :find "\"videoEnhanceQuality\""
     :replace "\"videoUpscale\""
     :must-fail ["every-pdcolor-task-type-is-served-by-a-graph-or-named-as-someone-elses"]}

    {:id :pdcolor/rights-gate-falls-through
     :why "PROCESS DATA. The rights gate's safety property is not that its condition is right, it is that a run answering NOTHING refuses. Point Gate_AutoRights' default at the human-approval branch and an unclassified work walks forward instead of blocking. One XML attribute; no test read it before"
     :file "bpmn/colorize-public-domain-work.bpmn"
     :find "<bpmn:exclusiveGateway id=\"Gate_AutoRights\" name=\"Rights class publishable?\" default=\"Flow_Rights_Blocked\">"
     :replace "<bpmn:exclusiveGateway id=\"Gate_AutoRights\" name=\"Rights class publishable?\" default=\"Flow_Rights_Human\">"
     :must-fail ["a-gate-nobody-answers-refuses"]}

    {:id :pdcolor/publish-bypasses-the-rights-gate
     :why "PROCESS DATA. A flow rerouted around a gate leaves every gate's own attributes correct -- the gate is still there, still fail-closed, and no longer on the path to Task_Publish. Only reachability sees it"
     :file "bpmn/colorize-public-domain-work.bpmn"
     :find "<bpmn:sequenceFlow id=\"Flow_SaveRun_Gate\" sourceRef=\"Task_SaveRun\" targetRef=\"Gate_AutoRights\"/>"
     :replace "<bpmn:sequenceFlow id=\"Flow_SaveRun_Gate\" sourceRef=\"Task_SaveRun\" targetRef=\"Task_HumanRightsApproval\"/>"
     :must-fail ["publish-is-behind-every-rights-and-qc-gate"]}

    {:id :pdcolor/blocked-run-rejoins-the-pipeline
     :why "PROCESS DATA. A blocked run must terminate. Sending the blocked audit back into the colorization chain gives a work that failed rights screening a path to publication, while every gate still refuses correctly on its own"
     :file "bpmn/colorize-public-domain-work.bpmn"
     :find "<bpmn:sequenceFlow id=\"Flow_EndBlocked\" sourceRef=\"Task_AuditBlocked\" targetRef=\"End_Blocked\"/>"
     :replace "<bpmn:sequenceFlow id=\"Flow_EndBlocked\" sourceRef=\"Task_AuditBlocked\" targetRef=\"Task_SegmentShots\"/>"
     :must-fail ["refusal-ends-the-process"]}

    {:id :pdcolor/runtimes-pin-different-langgraphs
     :why "RUNTIME CONFIG. nbb reads nbb.edn and the JVM reads deps.edn, so `both runtimes green` can quietly become `two runtimes, two libraries`. The replacement is a real adjacent langgraph commit, so the drift is what is caught rather than an unresolvable coordinate"
     :file "lg-clj/nbb.edn"
     :find "5fdc6e7d71d95bc78db4fa1a20c325c79940f984"
     :replace "bf75c16ac647d688e6a5dcef3bf2428e994256a0"
     :must-fail ["nbb-and-the-jvm-test-the-same-langgraph"]}

    {:id :pdcolor/camel-join-lowercases-the-rest
     :why "this one shoots the TEST, not the code. The BPMN-to-graph derivation is the test's own helper; `str/capitalize` lower-cases the rest, so segmentShots becomes Segmentshots and the mapping silently matches nothing. A `no unserved task types` assertion over an empty mapping would still be green"
     :file "lg-clj/test/lg_pd_color/contract_test.cljc"
     :find "(str (str/upper-case (subs s 0 1)) (subs s 1))"
     :replace "(str/capitalize s)"
     :must-fail ["the-derivation-is-not-vacuous"]}]}

  {:repo "orgs/cloud-itonami/business-person"
   :label "business-person planner: the gate, the envelope, the record key, and the manifest it must match"
   ;; src/business_person/murakumo.cljc is .cljc and had never been executed on
   ;; any runtime — the repo had no tests, no deps.edn, no nbb.edn. Every claim
   ;; about its gate was true only by inspection.
   ;;
   ;; All 18 were replayed by hand at pin 3edd2b8f on 2026-08-30 before landing,
   ;; one at a time with the tree restored between runs: every anchor unique,
   ;; every bite naming exactly the test that claims it and nothing else, base
   ;; green before the battery and after it.
   ;;
   ;; The first mutation written for `an-attestation-recorded-as-false-...` did
   ;; NOT bite. It aimed at `missing-gates`, whose `boolean` is redundant —
   ;; `gate-value`'s `or` chain has already turned an explicit false into nil,
   ;; so `boolean` and `some?` are equivalent there. The suite stayed green,
   ;; which is exactly what a vacuous test looks like from outside. The
   ;; registered mutation aims at `gate-value`, where the floor actually lives.
   ;;
   ;; Three tests are named hazard-* and pin DEFECTS, not guarantees: the rkey
   ;; collision, the caller-overwritable record body, and the DID document that
   ;; does not claim the DID this actor stamps. Their mutations are therefore
   ;; *fixes* — they go red when somebody repairs the defect, which is the
   ;; moment the test and the mutation should both be deleted.
   :cmd ["nbb" "test/run.cljs"]
   :green-marker "business-person: all green"
   :mutations
   [{:id :bp/an-attested-gate-is-normalised-to-true
     :why "an attestation recorded as false must not be read as attested. The floor is gate-value's `or`, not missing-gates' `boolean` — this normalises the lookup to a bare true and the false answer becomes a yes"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "  (or (get attestations gate)\n      (get attestations (name gate))"
     :replace "  (or (when (some? (get attestations gate)) true)\n      (get attestations (name gate))"
     :must-fail ["an-attestation-recorded-as-false-does-not-count-as-attested"]}

    {:id :bp/a-baseline-gate-is-dropped
     :why "dropping a gate from common-gates shrinks BOTH the required set and the expected set, so every set-equality assertion follows it down. Only the evidence floor on the count catches this"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "[:council-charter-attestation\n   :no-platform-held-key-baseline\n   :no-probing-baseline\n"
     :replace "[:council-charter-attestation\n   :no-platform-held-key-baseline\n"
     :must-fail ["the-planner-still-has-something-to-plan"]}

    {:id :bp/one-cell-quietly-requires-fewer-gates
     :why "the gate weakened for one cell out of twelve, which the fleet-wide count cannot see"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "  :koji {:legacy-cell \"koji\"\n     :phase :event\n     :murakumo-node \"reuben\"\n     :collections [(collection \"koji\")]\n     :required-gates common-gates"
     :replace "  :koji {:legacy-cell \"koji\"\n     :phase :event\n     :murakumo-node \"reuben\"\n     :collections [(collection \"koji\")]\n     :required-gates (vec (rest common-gates))"
     :must-fail ["every-cell-requires-every-common-gate"]}

    {:id :bp/blocked-plan-still-carries-records
     :why "a refusal that still hands back a planned :records body is a refusal a caller can walk around by not reading :status"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "         {:status :blocked\n          :effects []}"
     :replace "         {:status :blocked\n          :effects []\n          :records (vec (records-for spec input))}"
     :must-fail ["a-blocked-plan-carries-no-records-and-no-effects"]}

    {:id :bp/unknown-cell-returns-nil-instead-of-refusing
     :why "returning nil for an unknown cell key makes a typo indistinguishable from a cell that planned nothing — and the nil spec then plans :ready with no gates at all"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "    (when-not spec\n      (throw (ex-info \"unknown cell\" {:cell cell-key})))"
     :replace "    (when-not spec\n      nil)"
     :must-fail ["an-unknown-cell-is-refused-rather-than-planned"]}

    {:id :bp/effect-envelope-takes-the-actor-from-the-record
     :why "the envelope's :actor is the one field a caller must not be able to reach. Sourcing it from the record body hands the actor's identity to its input"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "{:op :mst/put-record\n   :actor actor-did"
     :replace "{:op :mst/put-record\n   :actor (or (:actorDid record) actor-did)"
     :must-fail ["a-caller-cannot-redirect-an-effect-envelope"]}

    {:id :bp/record-body-loses-the-actor-stamp
     :why "a record with no actorDid is a record nobody can attribute"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "        base {:actorDid actor-did\n              :computedAt computed-at"
     :replace "        base {:computedAt computed-at"
     :must-fail ["a-planned-record-carries-the-cells-own-provenance"]}

    {:id :bp/all-cell-plans-covers-only-the-first-cell
     :why "a planner that silently covers one cell of twelve reports success for eleven it never looked at"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "        (keys cell-specs)))"
     :replace "        (take 1 (keys cell-specs))))"
     :must-fail ["all-cell-plans-covers-every-cell-and-each-plan-names-its-own-cell"]}

    {:id :bp/rkey-lets-a-path-separator-through
     :why "a slash in a record key is not a degraded key, it is a different AT-URI path"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "(str/replace #\"[^A-Za-z0-9._~-]\" \"-\"))]"
     :replace "(str/replace #\"[^A-Za-z0-9._~/-]\" \"-\"))]"
     :must-fail ["safe-rkey-emits-only-atproto-legal-record-key-characters"]}

    {:id :bp/rkey-blank-fallback-removed
     :why "without the fallback an empty identifier yields an empty rkey, which is a malformed path rather than an anonymous record. Named twice because an empty string also fails the legality regex"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "    (if (str/blank? clean) \"unknown\" clean)))"
     :replace "    clean))"
     :must-fail ["safe-rkey-never-emits-an-empty-record-key"
                 "safe-rkey-emits-only-atproto-legal-record-key-characters"]}

    {:id :bp/did-web-strip-is-unanchored
     :why "the strip is anchored because did:web: appearing later in an identifier is data, not a prefix. Unanchored, it deletes from the middle"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find "(str/replace #\"^did:web:\" \"\")"
     :replace "(str/replace #\"did:web:\" \"\")"
     :must-fail ["safe-rkey-strips-the-did-web-prefix-only-at-the-start"]}

    {:id :bp/a-cell-writes-to-a-hand-edited-nsid
     :why "an NSID written out by hand instead of derived from the cell key does not fail here — the record lands in a collection nobody reads"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find ":collections [(collection \"person\")]"
     :replace ":collections [(collection \"persons\")]"
     :must-fail ["every-cell-writes-to-the-nsid-derived-from-its-own-key"]}

    {:id :bp/a-cell-is-renamed-without-the-manifest
     :why "the manifest subscribes to twelve things and the planner plans twelve things; rename one side and the actor stops covering a collection it is subscribed to. That does not fail here, it stalls in the broker"
     :file "src/business_person/murakumo.cljc"
     :find ":officerrole {:legacy-cell \"com-etzhayyim-apps-businessPerson-officerRole\""
     :replace ":officerrole {:legacy-cell \"com-etzhayyim-apps-businessPerson-officerRoles\""
