     :why "the subscribeRepos trigger is the one inbound path nobody calls deliberately -- records arrive from oilShipping whether or not this actor can plan for them. An unhandled collection is a silent drop, not an error"
     :file "actor-manifest.jsonld"
     :find "\"com.etzhayyim.apps.oilShipping.cargo\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"subscribeRepos\""
     :replace "\"com.etzhayyim.apps.oilShipping.manifest\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"subscribeRepos\""
     :must-fail ["every-subscribed-collection-has-a-cell-that-can-handle-it"]}

    {:id :oil/custom-escape-hatch-allowed
     :why "a step whose fn is outside the declared capability vocabulary runs with authority the manifest never granted. `custom` is the specific escape hatch the retired vitest file was written to refuse, so losing it would undo the one check that file was carried over for"
     :file "actor-manifest.jsonld"
     :find "\"fn\": \"derive:social\""
     :replace "\"fn\": \"custom\""
     :must-fail ["no-pipeline-step-escapes-into-a-custom-function"]}

    {:id :oil/served-did-document-is-reconciled
     :why "hazard tripwire. .well-known/did.json identifies itself as did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:oil-trading while the planner and the manifest both stamp did:web:oil-trading.etzhayyim.com, and alsoKnownAs bridges neither. Which side moves is an ownership decision; this fires whichever side moves first"
     :file ".well-known/did.json"
     :find "\"id\" : \"did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:oil-trading\","
     :replace "\"id\" : \"did:web:oil-trading.etzhayyim.com\","
     :must-fail ["hazard-the-served-did-document-does-not-claim-the-did-this-actor-stamps"]}

    {:id :oil/the-evidence-floor-itself
     :why "the floor under the suite, guarded like anything else. Dropping a namespace from the runner leaves a run that prints `0 failures, 0 errors` and would otherwise be read as a pass -- the exact shape ADR-2608136000 is about. It must exit 2, not 0 and not 1, and it must not print the marker. `must-fail` names the REFUSED line rather than a test, because the point is that no test ran"
     :file "run_tests.cljs"
     :find "(t/run-tests 'oil_trading.murakumo-test\n             'oil_trading.manifest-test)"
